## User preferences

- when decorative items are “để dùng cho mục đích trang trí bán trong cửa hàng” -> keep decoration-only items separate from gameplay powers, XP, production, or rewards. [Task 1]
- when the user corrected “ủa em còn 25 món h alloween chưa vẽ xong hả?” -> keep Halloween separate from special products, verify collection counts before reporting done, and proactively provide exact absolute paths and commit IDs when asked “em để đâu vậy”. [Task 2]
- when the user says “Duyệt bảng giá này và mở bán” and then “làm đi” -> direct approval of the exact table authorizes enabling sales and completing deployment; do not infer approval from prior plans. [Task 3]

## Reusable knowledge

- Decorations are cosmetic, one-time Galleons purchases with server-owned ownership/ledger mutations; placement/rotation is server-controlled. Existing source is vendored through `client/public/game/khu-vuon-hagrid/SOURCE.json`; use standalone `/Users/thachanh/Downloads/hagrid-farm`, not the vendored client. The special-products pack is local commit `c05209a`; its import handoff is `docs/special-products-import-handoff.md`. [Task 1]
- The Halloween `festival` collection is separate from the 30 `sp_*` special products. `garden-v05/halloween-assets/manifest.json` is the source of truth; integrate with `node garden-v05/special-products-assets/import-runtime.mjs garden-v05/halloween-assets festival`, importing only allowlisted native/frame files plus metadata. Do not ship masters, prompts, QA, thumbnails, or research logs. [Task 2]
- Final local package: 30 items/60 views, 300 native PNGs, 30 spritesheets, 120 thumbnails, and 450 verified hashes. Split masters at a transparent central gap, not equal half-widths; this prevents detached seam fragments. Preserve the five original seasonal masters byte-for-byte. [Task 2]
- The approved release enabled 25 new Halloween items totaling 90,400 G while preserving five existing Halloween IDs/prices. Catalog version `garden-2026-10-24-halloween-approved`, module `24.9.76`; scenario 1061 proved 25 purchases, debit/ledger totals, idempotent retries, wrong-price/off-season rejection, and ownership retention in an isolated emulator. [Task 3]
- Production proof was Cloud Run `hpvnn-client-production-00476-tnw` at 100% traffic with image/source `85ae8f24e`; all three aliases returned that commit, all six Hagrid Functions were ACTIVE, and unauthenticated calls returned 401. Revalidate live before reuse. [Task 3]

## Failures and how to do differently

- Do not treat the later special-products collection as a replacement for Halloween. [Task 1][Task 2]
- Symptom: two-view output has detached neighboring-view seam fragments. Cause: fixed half-width crop. Fix: split masters at a verified transparent central gap and audit source-pixel preservation before packaging. [Task 2]
- Asset QA alone does not prove runtime import, in-game rendering, phone QA, connected wallet, or production. This later release proved catalog/deployment behavior but still did not claim a real-wallet purchase or physical iPhone acceptance. [Task 2][Task 3]

